  "title": "Liuhe Pagoda, Hangzhou",
  "summary": "The Liuhe Pagoda stands at the foot of Yuelun Mountain in Hangzhou, Zhejiang. It was first built in the Northern Song period, lost in 1121 and rebuilt in 1165 under the Southern Song. The Hangzhou government gives its height as 59.89 metres, with a brick interior of seven storeys and a 13-storey outer timber form.",
